   - **Mechanical guards.** T232’s `config-census.md` lines 28 and 36 claim an application site and zero HITs. `recreation.html` line 32 declares `pipStyle`, and `codex/jev-prewave-2.md` line 14 identifies the missing read. Command 7 already classifies an unapplied key as a HIT. T212’s final prewave return finding 3 identifies unsupported fit minima, T218’s final return finding 3 identifies proxy measurements that diverge from final fitted geometry, and T219’s second return still calls for fit-summary reconciliation. Record the failed outputs against commands 6 and 7, with independent validation deferred under the HQ charge. A key-list diff alone would miss T232 because `pipStyle` appears in the census. The proposed regression case needs to verify that the claimed application site reads the value. Command 4 was not demanded because no lens scores exist.
   - **Jev definitions.** T218’s Observe-exit return gives both its lowest dimensions **0.5** and prints `RETURN-TO-OBSERVE · MECHANICS-UNSEEN`. `guards/jev-observe-exit.md` lines 27–32 give a strict **<0.5** floor and a separate guidance exception. Carry the classification basis as unresolved under the existing HQ deferral, alongside the prior FED-block and runner-binding debt. T218’s final prewave return also reports selected Node checks against the build, while `guards/jev-prewave.md` line 10 defines a paperwork judgment. Record that scope difference with the earlier deferred question. The substantive HOLD grounds can still stand.
   - **Codex prompts.** The **16** Phase A returns comprise **8 Codex** and **8 Jev** returns, computed as two of each per first attempt across four items. Cite the Codex findings and their dispositions separately, such as T219’s numerals-with-squares correction in Observe and T232’s timing-swap correction in Plan. Scoring was not demanded. Carry the stale “No run has fired” statements in `guards/codex-plan-review.md` and `guards/codex-condense.md` under the prior HQ deferral. Cycle 038 `RUN.md` §9.4 and §9b give the existing dispositions and reasons.

3. **Score-evidence binding — cite the returns where the lesson uses their numbers.** The final own-checks scores are **0.40, 0.45, 0.40, 0.45, 0.55**, in T212/T218/T219/T227/T232 order. Their range is **0.40–0.55**. Bind §9.1 directly to T212 `codex/jev-prewave-completion-cycle039.md`, T218 `codex/jev-prewave-refire.md`, local `item-T219-jev-prewave-2-return.md`, T227 `codex/jev-prewave-refire.md`, and T232 `codex/jev-prewave-2.md`. These are readiness scores. The five artifact `codex/` directories contain zero lens returns, so Cycle 039 has no lens-score lesson or verdict arithmetic to check. In §9.2, distinguish T218’s selected independent evaluation, T232’s CONFIG inspection, and T212’s arithmetic check on the supplied paperwork. [T219 final return](item-T219-jev-prewave-2-return.md)

4. **Wave re-pricing — correct §9.4.** The filed-return count before Condense is **25**, computed as **4 × 4 Phase A + 1 T212 completion + 4 × 2 first-attempt prewave**. That is **5 verdict-bearing gate returns per item** on average, with the restart-interrupted attempt disclosed separately. Firings per scored verdict are undefined. Elapsed per-item cost and the effect of changing wave size remain **UNASSESSED**. Section 0 compares **OWED + IN PROGRESS** with the **RECREATED pool**, so the draft’s comparison with recreated *movement* uses the wrong denominator. On the cycle’s reported counts, **12 + 2 = 14**, below the reported pool of **71**. The catalogue-wide test remains **UNVERIFIED** without a reconciled current census. Record the three-hour cadence as the schedule in force and leave any re-price unassessed. [INSTRUCTION.md §0](../../INSTRUCTION.md#0--cycle-shape-wave-form--throughput-correction-hq-2026-11-14)

