## Findings

1. **Amendment faithfulness — the deferral stands.** Cycle 039 claims no operative landing. `INSTRUCTION.md` §5 leg 3b still assigns receipt reconciliation to the builder, and `guards/guards.md` command 7 requires CONFIG-to-application-site resolution without prescribing an independent validator. Cycle 037 `RUN.md` §9b.1 already names both owning surfaces, the acceptance test, and HQ as consumer. Carry the deferral on **both** layers in Cycle 039 §9.3. Describe the pattern as recurring: Waves 34–36 cleared **0/5, 1/5, and 0/5**, respectively, from the five rows for each of Waves 34 and 35 in `verdict-history.md` and the five Wave 36 final returns. Wave 35 interrupts the zero-clearance streak. The returns establish that deficient receipts reached prewave after builder checks. The cause and the validator’s effectiveness remain unestablished. [Cycle 037 RUN.md](../2026-11-18-cycle-037-wave-34/RUN.md#9b--codex-condense-firing-1-dispositions-revise-applied-in-full) · [Cycle 039 RUN.md](RUN.md)

2. **Four-layer coverage — replace the blanket NO-DEFECT dispositions in §9.3 and the “solely” basis in §9.5.**
   - **Instruction steps.** T218’s Plan-review and Plan-exit payloads already contain a Plan and were filed before the Observe-exit return. That evidence contradicts the claim that the order held for all four first attempts. `INSTRUCTION.md` §1 requires the Observe-exit disposition before §2 opens. Record the T218 sequencing deviation separately from A9.2’s pre-build requirement, and carry the earlier sequencing disposition and the four-versus-five-lens conflict at `INSTRUCTION.md` §§2, 5, and 6.3. T218’s §2b gate-out also identifies continuous playback as set aside. Record the fine census and sibling-cure carry as the work actually done, with playback still outstanding under §1.2.
   - **Mechanical guards.** T232’s `config-census.md` lines 28 and 36 claim an application site and zero HITs. `recreation.html` line 32 declares `pipStyle`, and `codex/jev-prewave-2.md` line 14 identifies the missing read. Command 7 already classifies an unapplied key as a HIT. T212’s final prewave return finding 3 identifies unsupported fit minima, T218’s final return finding 3 identifies proxy measurements that diverge from final fitted geometry, and T219’s second return still calls for fit-summary reconciliation. Record the failed outputs against commands 6 and 7, with independent validation deferred under the HQ charge. A key-list diff alone would miss T232 because `pipStyle` appears in the census. The proposed regression case needs to verify that the claimed application site reads the value. Command 4 was not demanded because no lens scores exist.
   - **Jev definitions.** T218’s Observe-exit return gives both its lowest dimensions **0.5** and prints `RETURN-TO-OBSERVE · MECHANICS-UNSEEN`. `guards/jev-observe-exit.md` lines 27–32 give a strict **<0.5** floor and a separate guidance exception. Carry the classification basis as unresolved under the existing HQ deferral, alongside the prior FED-block and runner-binding debt. T218’s final prewave return also reports selected Node checks against the build, while `guards/jev-prewave.md` line 10 defines a paperwork judgment. Record that scope difference with the earlier deferred question. The substantive HOLD grounds can still stand.
