3. **Score-evidence binding — cite the returns where the lesson uses their numbers.** The final own-checks scores are **0.40, 0.45, 0.40, 0.45, 0.55**, in T212/T218/T219/T227/T232 order. Their range is **0.40–0.55**. Bind §9.1 directly to T212 `codex/jev-prewave-completion-cycle039.md`, T218 `codex/jev-prewave-refire.md`, local `item-T219-jev-prewave-2-return.md`, T227 `codex/jev-prewave-refire.md`, and T232 `codex/jev-prewave-2.md`. These are readiness scores. The five artifact `codex/` directories contain zero lens returns, so Cycle 039 has no lens-score lesson or verdict arithmetic to check. In §9.2, distinguish T218’s selected independent evaluation, T232’s CONFIG inspection, and T212’s arithmetic check on the supplied paperwork. [T219 final return](item-T219-jev-prewave-2-return.md)

4. **Wave re-pricing — correct §9.4.** The filed-return count before Condense is **25**, computed as **4 × 4 Phase A + 1 T212 completion + 4 × 2 first-attempt prewave**. That is **5 verdict-bearing gate returns per item** on average, with the restart-interrupted attempt disclosed separately. Firings per scored verdict are undefined. Elapsed per-item cost and the effect of changing wave size remain **UNASSESSED**. Section 0 compares **OWED + IN PROGRESS** with the **RECREATED pool**, so the draft’s comparison with recreated *movement* uses the wrong denominator. On the cycle’s reported counts, **12 + 2 = 14**, below the reported pool of **71**. The catalogue-wide test remains **UNVERIFIED** without a reconciled current census. Record the three-hour cadence as the schedule in force and leave any re-price unassessed. [INSTRUCTION.md §0](../../INSTRUCTION.md#0--cycle-shape-wave-form--throughput-correction-hq-2026-11-14)

